 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Not rude, just not common. Most families expect to treat their guests. Then treat them as guests, not hosts. Offer to share your kitchen but not your pocketbook. Say something like, We'd love to share our kitchen, but we' short on space. Would you rather come home to empty boxes, or eat at the local pub every night? Actively listen, and say, I respect your wish for independence, but I also want make you welcome. Is there another way you'd like to structure the visits?",
